msgid "Desktop and web"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*What differs between the desktop application and EMStudio served by a "
"StratiGraph node.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EMStudio is one application with two ways of reaching it. The **desktop "
"application** runs on macOS, Windows and Linux and brings its own local "
"helper, the *bridge*, which reads and writes the files of this computer. "
"The **web version** is the same editor served by a StratiGraph node at "
"the address ``/em/studio/`` of that node: you reach it with a browser and"
" sign in to the node."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The windows, the workspaces, the graph and almost every command are the "
"same in both. They differ where a browser and a desktop program are "
"different by nature: a page in a browser receives the content of a file "
"but never learns where the file lives on the disk, it cannot choose a "
"folder through the system's dialog, and it saves by downloading. The "
"table below lists every difference of version 1.6.0-dev.136, grouped by "
"theme."
msgstr ""

msgid "Area"
msgstr ""

msgid "Desktop"
msgstr ""

msgid "Web"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Open…**, also with **Replace the open files**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The system's dialog opens. EMStudio keeps the path of the file, so it can"
" save it in place and reopen it later."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The browser's file picker opens. EMStudio receives the content of the "
"file without its path."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Save**"
msgstr "**Speichern**"

msgid ""
"The file is written in its place on the disk. A file that came from a "
"drop or from a room has no place yet, so the first **Save** asks for one."
msgstr ""

msgid "The em.json is downloaded by the browser."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Save As…**"
msgstr "**Speichern unter…**"

msgid ""
"The system's dialog proposes the file's own folder. In another folder, "
"EMStudio offers to rewrite the paths of the resources so that they still "
"point at the same files."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The em.json is downloaded under a new name. A dialog reminds you that its"
" resource paths are relative to the folder where you keep it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Open Recent ▸**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A recent file reopens from its path. A file that has disappeared is said "
"so, and you can remove it from the list."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A file dropped into the browser has no path: drag it in again to reopen "
"it. A recent room reopens on both platforms."
msgstr ""

msgid "Files given at launch, and files dropped from the system"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Files opened with EMStudio from the system, and files or folders dropped "
"on the window, arrive with their path."
msgstr ""

msgid "A file dropped on the page arrives as its content only."
msgstr ""

msgid "**New EM project…** and **Open project…**"
msgstr ""

msgid "The system's folder dialog opens."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EMStudio's own folder selector opens inside the page, starting from the "
"folder that the **Files** window is showing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choosing a folder in the **Files** window, and **another folder…**"
msgstr ""

msgid "The system's folder dialog."
msgstr ""

msgid "EMStudio's own folder selector, or a path that you type."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Find missing files…**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can add one more folder to the search through the system's dialog, "
"and point a missing file at its new place by choosing it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The folder to search is given as a path that you type; a missing file is "
"pointed at its new place through EMStudio's own selector."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Bring in…** ▸ **Files…**"
msgstr ""

msgid "The system's dialog lets you choose several files at once."
msgstr ""

msgid "EMStudio's own selector lets you choose one file at a time."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Import ▸ GraphML…**, **Import ▸ Table with a mapping…**, **StratiMiner**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The system's dialog returns the file with its path. A GraphML matrix kept"
" as em.json is saved beside the GraphML."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The browser hands the file over and the bridge keeps a working copy. A "
"GraphML matrix kept as em.json is downloaded under the name you give."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Export ▸ Turtle (.ttl)**, the files an extension exports"
msgstr ""

msgid "Saved where you choose."
msgstr ""

msgid "Downloaded."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Colours…**: the colour schemes of the file"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Written into a folder that you choose, and read from several files at "
"once."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Written into the browser's downloads, and read through the browser's file"
" picker."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Print sheets…**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Print…** opens the system's print dialog, which also makes the PDF "
"(**Save as PDF**). **One PDF per sheet** needs a bridge that makes PDFs; "
"the installed application makes its PDF through the print dialog."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Print…** prints the preview through the browser's print dialog, which "
"also makes the single PDF. When the node makes PDFs, one PDF per sheet is"
" downloaded file by file."
msgstr ""

msgid "The title of the window"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shows the open file, with a dot when it has unsaved changes."
msgstr ""

msgid "The browser's tab keeps its own title."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Open in a new window**"
msgstr ""

msgid "The window becomes a window of the system, kept above the main window."
msgstr ""

msgid "The window becomes a separate browser window."
msgstr ""

msgid "Signing in to a node (the chip's menu, **Node and account**)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The sign-in runs in the system's browser and comes back to the "
"application; when it does not, the node's answer is pasted in **Paste the"
" node's answer**. EMStudio asks to sign in only when you ask."
msgstr ""

msgid "The sign-in runs in the same page. EMStudio can renew it quietly."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Verify with ORCID**"
msgstr ""

msgid "The application goes straight to ORCID."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On the node's default configuration, the verification goes through the "
"node's own ORCID sign-in."
msgstr ""

msgid "The node"
msgstr ""

msgid "None until you configure one in **Settings… ▸ Connections**."
msgstr ""

msgid "The node that serves the page, found from the page's own address."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**My space on the node**, and pages opened by **Open with…** "
"(StratiField, Heriverse)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Opened in the system's browser."
msgstr ""

msgid "Opened in a new tab of the browser."
msgstr ""

msgid "Nodes on the local network, and the personal node of this computer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The bridge searches the local network and can turn on a node on this "
"computer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The search of the local network belongs to the bridge of the desktop "
"application. The saved nodes and the address you type are checked."
msgstr ""

msgid "The AI key (**Settings… ▸ Advanced ▸ API key**)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Kept in the system's keychain."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kept by the bridge for the session."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Pack this tileset into a .3tz**"
msgstr ""

msgid "Available."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Available in the **Files** window for a folder served by the helper "
"service, which writes the archive. A tileset of your own computer is "
"packed in the desktop application."
msgstr ""

msgid "The hardware profile of the **Space** (**Use of this device**)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Read as *desktop* on a machine with a graphics card: the scene loads the "
"realtime versions of the models."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Read as *web*: the scene loads the versions made for the web. You can "
"change the profile by hand on both."
msgstr ""

msgid "``Settings… ▸ Extensions`` ▸ **Install from disk…**"
msgstr ""

msgid "From a .zip archive or from a folder."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Served by a node, the page lists the packages that the node's "
"administrator installed; the page installs nothing."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Repositories of extensions in a folder (for example on a NAS), and the "
"development folder of a plugin"
msgstr ""

msgid "Chosen through the system's folder dialog."
msgstr ""

msgid "These folders belong to the desktop application."
msgstr ""

msgid "Plugins of your own computer, and ``Tools ▸ Python console…``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The plugins installed on the node, turned on for the room, run on the "
"node; plugins and the console of a computer belong to the desktop "
"application."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Check for updates…**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In **Help** on Windows and Linux, in the **EMStudio** menu on macOS. "
"EMStudio compares its version with the published releases, and offers "
"**Download** and, where it can, **Install and restart**."
msgstr ""

msgid "The version is the one the node serves."
msgstr ""

msgid "Menus"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On macOS the system's menu bar carries **File**, **Edit** and **Help**, "
"plus the **EMStudio** menu (**About EMStudio**, **Settings…**, **Check "
"for updates…**) and the **Window** menu. On Windows and Linux the menu "
"bar is inside the window, and **File** ends with **Quit EMStudio**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The menu bar is inside the page. **About EMStudio** and **Settings…** are"
" in **Help**."
msgstr ""

msgid "Keys"
msgstr ""

msgid ":kbd:`⌘` on macOS, :kbd:`Ctrl` on Windows and Linux."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The same keys, except those the browser keeps for itself: **Close** has "
"no key on the web, because :kbd:`⌘W` and :kbd:`Ctrl+W` close the "
"browser's tab."
msgstr ""

msgid "How the manual marks the differences"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The manual describes the two platforms with one text. Where the steps of "
"a task really diverge, a page shows two tabs, **Desktop** and **Web**: "
"choose yours once, and every page of the manual follows your choice. "
"Where the steps are the same, there are no tabs."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the reference tables, *desktop only* marks a command that the web "
"version does not draw (see :doc:`menus`). A difference among macOS, "
"Windows and Linux is said in the text of the **Desktop** tab."
msgstr ""

